            },
            "description": "Rewrites follow-up Billing questions into standalone semantic requests using prior Billing context without changing literal identifiers.",
            "errorNodeId": "1779832851336",
            "name": "Resolve Billing Semantic Context"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770000001002"
          },
          "code": "RESOLVE_BILLING_SEMANTIC_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1770000001020",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770000001020_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the semantic context resolver for the Oracle Receivables Billing Inquiry Assistant. Return JSON only. Do not answer the user's business question.\n\nInputs:\n- raw_user_input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- prior_billing_context: {{$context.$variables.billingContext}}\n- prior_semantic_rewrite: {{$context.$variables.billingSemanticRewrite}}\n- pending_billing_semantic_rewrite: {{$context.$variables.pendingBillingSemanticRewrite}}\n- prior_billing_chatcontent: {{$context.$variables.billingChatContent}}\n- chat_history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nTask:\nRewrite the current user message into one standalone Receivables Billing inquiry sentence that downstream intent classification can use.\n\nRules:\n- Preserve literal identifiers exactly, including invoice numbers, sales orders, PO numbers, customer names, account numbers, credit memo numbers, dispute/request ids, adjustment numbers, punctuation, case, leading zeroes, underscores, slashes, and hyphens.\n- If the current user message contains a new explicit identifier, use the current identifier and do not overwrite it from prior context.\n- If the prior turn asked a clarification and the current user only names the reference type, combine that type with pending_billing_semantic_rewrite instead of inventing a new value.\n- Use prior_billing_chatcontent only as structured context for true follow-ups or clarification answers; never let it override a current explicit anchor.\n- If the current user message is a follow-up such as \"what about tax\", \"has it been paid\", \"who approved it\", \"show lines\", \"send copy\", or \"what about due date\", \"what about deferred revenue\", or \"show the earning schedule\", carry forward the missing invoice/customer/account/order context from prior_billing_context.\n- If there is no usable prior context for a follow-up, keep the user's question as-is and mark usedPriorContext false.\n- Do not add new facts, amounts, dates, statuses, tax reasons, or explanations.\n- Keep the rewrite in scope-neutral wording. Tax lookup is allowed, but tax advice, tax law, and root-cause tax determination are not.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON shape:\n{\"semanticRewrite\":\"standalone billing inquiry sentence\",\"usedPriorContext\":false,\"contextSummary\":\"short note or empty string\"}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"semanticRewrite\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"usedPriorContext\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"contextSummary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"semanticRewrite\",\n    \"usedPriorContext\",\n    \"contextSummary\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
