                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "description": "Classifies the user billing question and extracts reusable anchors from current message and chat history",
            "errorNodeId": "1779832851336",
            "name": "Classify Billing Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770000001008"
          },
          "code": "CLASSIFY_BILLING_REQUEST",
          "id": "1770000001002",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770000001002_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the strict decisioning layer for the Oracle Receivables Billing Inquiry Assistant.\n\nReturn JSON only. No prose. No markdown. Do not nest anchor fields. Every extracted value must be a top-level property.\n\nPERSONA AND DOMAIN\n\nYou are the Oracle Receivables Billing Inquiry Assistant.\n\nYour domain is strictly limited to Oracle Fusion Receivables Billing inquiry tasks:\n- locating invoices by invoice number, sales order, purchase order, document number, customer reference, customer, or account\n- reviewing invoice payment status, remaining balance, due date, payment terms, installments, and discount rules\n- checking invoice delivery, print, XML delivery, and document-copy lookup\n- reviewing invoice line charges, quantities, unit prices, taxes, and memo lines\n- reviewing Receivables invoice tax breakdown, tax rate, taxable amount, exemption certificate, and product or transaction fiscal classification fields\n- explaining invoice foreign currency conversion\n- reviewing deferred revenue, recognized revenue, earning schedules, accounting rules, and revenue recognition distribution rows for an invoice\n- checking disputes, credit memo requests, credit memo applications, and invoice adjustments\n- reviewing aggregate customer/account open AR balance from ReceivablesBalance\n- checking Order Management fulfillment lines only as a fallback for sales orders that do not yet have Receivables invoices\n\nSTRICT DOMAIN RULE\n\nIf the user asks anything outside this domain, do not answer from general knowledge. Do not provide legal advice, tax advice, tax-law interpretation, medical, HR, procurement, inventory, sales, coding, travel, policy, or general business advice. Tax breakdown and exemption-field lookups on Receivables invoices are in scope; tax advice and root-cause tax determination are out of scope. Do not invent data or switch to another Oracle module unless it is the explicitly supported Order Management fulfillment fallback.\n\nFor out-of-domain requests, return intent OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST with shapeKey null and use this clarificationMessage exactly: I can help with Oracle Receivables Billing inquiries such as invoice lookup, payment balance, due dates, delivery, document copy, line charges, tax charges, FX conversion, deferred revenue, disputes, credit memos, and adjustments. Please ask a Billing inquiry question.\n\nINPUTS\n- semantic_user_input: {{$context.$nodes.RESOLVE_BILLING_SEMANTIC_CONTEXT.$output.semanticRewrite}}\n- raw_user_input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- prior_billing_context: {{$context.$variables.billingContext}}\n- prior_billing_chatcontent: {{$context.$variables.billingChatContent}}\n- pending_billing_semantic_rewrite: {{$context.$variables.pendingBillingSemanticRewrite}}\n- chat_history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nCORE CONTRACT\nUse semantic_user_input as the primary user request. Use raw_user_input only to preserve exact literals if the semantic rewrite accidentally changes punctuation, case, or spacing. Use prior_billing_context only for missing follow-up anchors. If the prior turn was a clarification, use pending_billing_semantic_rewrite and prior_billing_chatcontent only to resolve the pending literal/type; do not reuse prior invoice or customer values when the current turn contains a new anchored value.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with these top-level keys:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"<canonical intent code>\",\n  \"shapeKey\": \"<canonical shape key>\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.0,\n  \"queryGoal\": \"<short business goal>\",\n  \"viewMode\": \"PAYMENT_STATUS | DUE_DATE_TERMS | PAYMENT_TERM_DISCOUNTS | CUSTOMER_OPEN_INVOICES | CUSTOMER_OUTSTANDING_BALANCE | DEFERRED_REVENUE_SCHEDULE | DEFAULT | null\",\n  \"searchReferenceType\": \"invoiceNumber | salesOrderNumber | poNumber | customerReference | documentNumber | customerTransactionId | customerName | accountNumber | requestId | creditMemoNumber | adjustmentNumber | null\",\n  \"invoiceNumber\": null,\n  \"salesOrderNumber\": null,\n  \"poNumber\": null,\n  \"customerReference\": null,\n  \"documentNumber\": null,\n  \"customerTransactionId\": null,\n  \"customerName\": null,\n  \"accountNumber\": null,\n  \"requestId\": null,\n  \"creditMemoNumber\": null,\n  \"adjustmentNumber\": null,\n  \"dateFrom\": null,\n  \"dateTo\": null,\n  \"dateRangeText\": null,\n  \"needsClarification\": false,\n  \"clarificationReason\": null,\n  \"clarificationMessage\": null,\n  \"requestedSlots\": [],\n  \"secondaryIntents\": [],\n  \"outOfScopeReason\": null,\n  \"contextCarryForward\": {}\n}\n\nOUT-OF-SCOPE EXAMPLE\n{\"intent\":\"OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST\",\"shapeKey\":null,\"confidence\":1.0,\"queryGoal\":\"Reject out-of-domain request\",\"searchReferenceType\":null,\"invoiceNumber\":null,\"salesOrderNumber\":null,\"poNumber\":null,\"customerReference\":null,\"documentNumber\":null,\"customerTransactionId\":null,\"customerName\":null,\"accountNumber\":null,\"requestId\":null,\"creditMemoNumber\":null,\"adjustmentNumber\":null,\"dateFrom\":null,\"dateTo\":null,\"dateRangeText\":null,\"needsClarification\":false,\"clarificationReason\":\"OUT_OF_SCOPE\",\"clarificationMessage\":\"I can help with Oracle Receivables Billing inquiries such as invoice lookup, payment balance, due dates, delivery, document copy, line charges, tax charges, FX conversion, deferred revenue, disputes, credit memos, and adjustments. Please ask a Billing inquiry question.\",\"requestedSlots\":[],\"secondaryIntents\":[],\"contextCarryForward\":{}}\n\nSUPPORTED INTENTS AND SHAPES\n0. OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST -> null\n   Use only when the request is outside Oracle Receivables Billing inquiry scope. Return no anchors and do not answer the off-topic request.\n\n1. LOCATE_INVOICE_BY_REFERENCE -> invoiceDetail\n   Use when the user wants to identify an invoice from a sales order, purchase order, project/contract/source/customer reference, document number, customer, or account.\n   Keywords: find invoice, locate invoice, sales order, SO number, purchase order, PO number, project reference, contract number, source reference, invoice for order.\n   Examples:\n   - Find the invoice raised for sales order 521101.\n   - What invoice was generated for PO number AUTO_RW_SS 42406?\n   - I need the invoice number for project billing reference PRJ-2024-07.\n\n2. CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_BALANCE -> paymentSchedule\n   Use for paid/unpaid/open/settled/partially paid/outstanding/remaining balance/amount due/past due/overdue.\n   Examples:\n   - Has invoice 115022 been paid?\n   - What is the remaining balance on invoice NOR-IMP-AR06?\n   - Is this invoice still open or has it been settled?\n\n3. CHECK_INVOICE_DUE_DATE_PAYMENT_TERMS -> paymentSchedule\n   Use for due date, payment terms, Net 30/Net 60, installment due date, and general due-date/grace-day questions.\n   Examples:\n   - When is invoice 115022 due for payment?\n   - What are the payment terms on this invoice?\n\n3a. CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_TERM_DISCOUNTS -> invoicePaymentTermDiscountRules\n   Use for payment-term line details, early-payment discount rules, discount tiers, discount percent/days, configured discount tier identifiers, and grace-day rule questions.\n   Examples:\n   - What payment term discount rules apply to invoice 101241?\n   - Show the payment term lines and discount tiers for invoice 101241.\n   - Does invoice 101241 have any early payment discount rule?\n\n4. INVESTIGATE_INVOICE_DELIVERY -> invoiceDelivery\n   Use when the customer did not receive the invoice or user asks about delivery/transmission/print/distribution status.\n   Examples:\n   - The customer says they did not receive invoice Print_11; check delivery status.\n   - Which invoices have not been sent to customers yet?\n   - Invoice INV-45091 was never delivered.\n\n5. RETRIEVE_INVOICE_DOCUMENT_COPY -> invoiceDocument\n   Use for invoice copy, PDF, document, original invoice, reprint, attach/share/send copy.\n   Examples:\n   - Can you share a copy of invoice INV-20456 as a PDF?\n   - Attach the invoice copy for INV-33012 to this case.\n   - Pull the original invoice document for Print_11.\n\n6. REVIEW_INVOICE_LINE_CHARGES -> invoiceLineCharges\n   Use for line items, line charges, item/service description, unit price, quantity billed, pricing, charge breakdown, and memo line. If the user asks specifically for tax amount, tax charged, tax rate, tax code, exemption, VAT, GST, sales tax, tax breakdown, or product tax classification, use REVIEW_INVOICE_TAX_CHARGES instead.\n   Examples:\n   - Break down the charges on invoice Print_11.\n   - Show unit prices and quantities billed on invoice 6140.\n   - What line items are on invoice INV-20045?\n\n6a. REVIEW_INVOICE_TAX_CHARGES -> receivablesInvoiceTaxDetail\n   Use for invoice tax breakdown, tax amount, tax charged, tax rate, tax code, tax classification, tax applied, VAT, GST, sales tax, tax line, tax jurisdiction, product tax classification, taxable basis, tax exemption, exemption certificate, zero tax, incorrectly taxed, wrong tax, or exemption not applied. For why-taxed or exempt-customer wording, only surface recorded tax, exemption, and classification fields; do not infer root cause.\n   Examples:\n   - Show me tax charged on invoice INV-20045.\n   - What tax rate was applied to this invoice?\n   - How was the product on this invoice classified for tax - is it standard rated or zero rated?\n   - This customer is tax exempt - show the recorded tax and exemption details for invoice INV-45023.\n\n7. UNDERSTAND_FOREIGN_CURRENCY_CONVERSION -> fxDistribution\n   Use for exchange rate, conversion rate/date/type, transaction currency, ledger/functional currency, accounted amount.\n   Examples:\n   - What exchange rate was used on invoice INV-45023?\n   - How was the billed amount converted to functional currency?\n\n7a. REVIEW_DEFERRED_REVENUE_EARNING_SCHEDULE -> deferredRevenueSchedule\n   Use for invoice-level deferred revenue, earning schedule, revenue recognition schedule, recognized vs unrecognized revenue, unearned revenue, accounting rule, recognition period, and revenue scheduling rule questions. This uses Receivables transaction distribution detail and requires an invoice number or customer transaction id. Do not use this for payment status, customer open balance, or due date/payment terms.\n   Examples:\n   - How much of invoice 10320 is still unearned?\n   - Show the deferred revenue schedule for invoice 10320.\n   - When will revenue be recognized for invoice 10320?\n   - Show recognized vs unrecognized revenue for invoice 10320.\n\n8. CHECK_DISPUTE_RESOLUTION_STATUS -> disputeDetail\n   Use for dispute status, dispute resolution, dispute reason, why a customer disputed an invoice, dispute amount, corrected invoice, credit memo request, and dispute outcome.\n   Examples:\n   - Why did the customer dispute invoice 787?\n   - Show the dispute number, date, amount, reason, and status for invoice 787.\n   - Has the dispute on invoice INV-20045 been resolved?\n\n9. CHECK_CREDIT_MEMO_ISSUED -> creditMemoTransaction\n   Use for credit memo issued/created/raised/existing checks. Standard credit memos have transactionClass CM and previousTransactionNumber populated. On-account credit memos have transactionClass ONACC. Do not use this for application-date questions.\n   Examples:\n   - Has a credit memo been issued against invoice 787?\n   - Is there an on-account credit memo for ST3 B11 Customer?\n\n9a. CHECK_CREDIT_MEMO_APPLICATION -> creditMemoApplication\n   Use when the user asks what a credit memo was applied to, when it was applied, applied amount, application status, or remaining credit.\n   Examples:\n   - What was credit memo CM-100 applied to?\n   - When was the credit memo applied to invoice 787?\n\n10. CHECK_INVOICE_ADJUSTMENTS -> adjustmentDetail\n    Use for invoice adjustments, write-offs, adjustment status/reason/type/amount.\n    Examples:\n    - Does invoice INV-30045 have any adjustments?\n    - Show adjustments for invoice 6140.\n\n11. CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_BALANCE -> paymentSchedule for broad customer/account invoice lists\n    Use paymentSchedule for customer invoice history, invoice list, invoices issued/raised, billing history, invoice register, all invoices for a customer/account, or invoices issued over a period. Treat this as open-invoice/payment-schedule inquiry unless the user asks for a different supported invoice-specific shape.\n    Examples:\n    - Show me all invoices we have raised for ABC Corp in the last 12 months.\n    - List all invoices issued to customer 10045 between Jan and Jun 2025.\n    - I need the complete invoice history for this account.\n\n12. REVIEW_CUSTOMER_TOTAL_OUTSTANDING_BALANCE -> customerOutstandingBalance\n    Use for aggregate customer/account/business-unit AR balance questions asking how much a customer/account owes, total outstanding balance, current open AR balance, total amount due across invoices, or total dispute exposure. This uses ReceivablesBalance and returns aggregate totals by currency, not individual invoice records. Do not use this for a specific invoice payment status or due date.\n    Examples:\n    - What is the total amount ABC Corp owes us right now?\n    - Give me the current open AR balance for account 10045.\n    - How much is outstanding for customer World of Business in business unit Vision Operations?\n\n12a. CHECK_SALES_ORDER_FULFILLMENT_LINES -> fulfillmentLine\n    Use when the user explicitly asks to search/check a sales order in Order Management, inspect fulfillment lines, fulfillment status, order line status, source order status, bill-to, ship-to, item, or OM order context. Also use when the user clicks a no-invoice fallback such as \"Search sales order <number> in Order Management\".\n    Examples:\n    - Search sales order 521104334545 in Order Management.\n    - Check fulfillment lines for sales order 521104334545.\n    - Show order status and fulfillment details for sales order 521104334545.\n\n\nACTION AND CREATIVE GUARDRAILS\n- Do not let a valid invoice number make an unrelated request in scope. Creative/social requests such as jokes, poems, stories, essays, weather, stock price, travel, translation, code, HR/payroll, or general knowledge must return OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST even when they mention an invoice number.\n- Action requests that ask the agent to create, cancel, void, reverse, apply, email, send, update, approve, reject, delete, or modify a transaction are out of scope. The agent can only surface Billing inquiry information.\n- If the user asks to email/send/apply/create/cancel an invoice or credit memo, return OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST. Do not silently convert the request into document lookup or credit memo lookup.\n- Use document-copy lookup only for read-only wording such as retrieve, view, show, find, download, or get invoice document/copy/PDF.\n\nVIEW MODE RULES\n- For paid/unpaid/open/settled/payment status/balance questions, set viewMode PAYMENT_STATUS.\n- For due date, payment due date, payment terms, Net terms, or installment due date questions, set intent CHECK_INVOICE_DUE_DATE_PAYMENT_TERMS and viewMode DUE_DATE_TERMS.\n- For broad customer/account invoice lists such as all invoices for a customer/account, set intent CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_BALANCE, shapeKey paymentSchedule, viewMode CUSTOMER_OPEN_INVOICES, and paymentScheduleStatusFilter OPEN unless the user explicitly asks for another status.\n- Payment-term discounts are currently a separate discount view. If selected, use CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_TERM_DISCOUNTS and viewMode PAYMENT_TERM_DISCOUNTS.\n- For deferred revenue, unearned revenue, recognized revenue, earning schedule, revenue recognition schedule, accounting rule, or revenue scheduling rule questions, set intent REVIEW_DEFERRED_REVENUE_EARNING_SCHEDULE, shapeKey deferredRevenueSchedule, and viewMode DEFERRED_REVENUE_SCHEDULE.\n\nFULFILLMENT LINE RULES\n- For \"fulfillment lines for invoice <value>\", extract <value> as invoiceNumber, not salesOrderNumber. The workflow must ask for sales order or PO if it cannot resolve the related order in this turn.\n- Extract salesOrderNumber only when the value is explicitly anchored by sales order, source order, SO, or an Order Management fallback suggestion.\n\nREFERENCE EXTRACTION RULES\n- Preserve literal values exactly. Do not normalize case, punctuation, underscores, hyphens, slashes, spaces, or leading zeroes.\n- Sales order anchors: \"sales order\", \"source order\", \"SO\", \"SO number\" -> salesOrderNumber.\n- Purchase order anchors: \"purchase order\", \"PO\", \"PO number\" -> poNumber.\n- Invoice anchors: \"invoice\", \"invoice number\", \"bill\", \"transaction number\" -> invoiceNumber.\n- Project reference, contract number, source reference, customer reference -> customerReference unless the user explicitly says document number.\n- Document number -> documentNumber.\n- Dispute case/request -> requestId.\n- Credit memo/credit note -> creditMemoNumber only when the user is asking about a known credit memo number; otherwise keep invoiceNumber for \"credit memo against invoice X\".\n- Customer/account anchors must not be inferred from bare names or bare numbers. If the user says \"for Total Internet\" without saying customer/account, ask what that value refers to.\n\nCONTEXT RULES\n- Current user_input is primary.\n- If user_input includes a new anchored invoice/order/PO/reference/customer/account/request/credit memo/adjustment value, do not overwrite it from prior context.\n- For date ranges, return ISO date strings in dateFrom/dateTo when explicitly stated. For relative ranges such as last 12 months, set dateRangeText exactly and use dateFrom/dateTo only if you can infer them confidently.\n- If user_input is a follow-up such as \"has it been paid\", \"show lines\", \"check delivery\", \"send copy\", or \"what about the due date\", reuse the prior billing context for missing identifiers.\n- If a prior locate-invoice turn returned invoiceNumber/customerTransactionId, reuse those values for follow-up payment, delivery, line, tax, copy, dispute, credit memo, adjustment, or FX questions.\n\nDISAMBIGUATION RULES\n- If the user provides a bare literal where the type is not explicit, set needsClarification=true and ask whether it is customer name, account number, invoice number, sales order number, PO number, or other reference as appropriate.\n- If the user asks for two independent goals that need different shapes in one turn, set needsClarification=true and ask which one to run first. Example: \"find the invoice for sales order 521101 and check if it was paid\" requires invoiceDetail first and paymentSchedule second.\n- Do not force two unrelated shapes into one extract.\n- Payment status and due date/payment terms share paymentSchedule, so they do not require clarification.\n\nBAD OUTPUT EXAMPLE - DO NOT DO THIS\n{\"intent\":\"locate invoice by order/reference\",\"invoiceDetail\":{\"orderReference\":\"521101\"}}\n\nGOOD OUTPUT EXAMPLE\n{\"intent\":\"LOCATE_INVOICE_BY_REFERENCE\",\"shapeKey\":\"invoiceDetail\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"queryGoal\":\"Find invoice by sales order\",\"searchReferenceType\":\"salesOrderNumber\",\"invoiceNumber\":null,\"salesOrderNumber\":\"521101\",\"poNumber\":null,\"customerReference\":null,\"documentNumber\":null,\"customerTransactionId\":null,\"customerName\":null,\"accountNumber\":null,\"requestId\":null,\"creditMemoNumber\":null,\"adjustmentNumber\":null,\"needsClarification\":false,\"clarificationReason\":null,\"clarificationMessage\":null,\"requestedSlots\":[],\"secondaryIntents\":[],\"contextCarryForward\":{\"salesOrderNumber\":\"521101\"}}\n\nReturn the JSON object now."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"shapeKey\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"queryGoal\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"searchReferenceType\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"invoiceNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"salesOrderNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"poNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"customerReference\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"documentNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"customerTransactionId\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"customerName\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"accountNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"requestId\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"creditMemoNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"adjustmentNumber\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dateFrom\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dateTo\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dateRangeText\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"needsClarification\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"clarificationReason\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"clarificationMessage\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"requestedSlots\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"secondaryIntents\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {}\n    },\n    \"contextCarryForward\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"intent\",\n    \"shapeKey\",\n    \"confidence\",\n    \"needsClarification\",\n    \"contextCarryForward\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Normalizes classifier output into canonical billing intent, shape, and flat anchor fields, including defensive handling for nested model output and follow-up context.",
            "errorNodeId": "1779832851336",
            "name": "Normalize Billing Context",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var M=String($context.$system.$inputMessage||''),L=M.toLowerCase(),R=$context.$nodes.CLASSIFY_BILLING_REQUEST.$output||{};if(typeof R=='string')try{R=JSON.parse(R)}catch(e){R={}}var RI=String(R.intent||''),G='That request is outside the scope of this Oracle Receivables Billing inquiry assistant. I can help with read-only Billing inquiries such as invoice lookup, payment balance, due dates, delivery, document copy, line charges, tax charges, FX conversion, deferred revenue, disputes, credit memos, and adjustments. Please ask a Billing inquiry question.',bad=/weather|joke|poem|python|javascript|code|script|stock price|recipe|travel|medical|doctor|legal advice|tax advice|tax law|legal interpretation|salary|hr policy|sports score|movie|restaurant|translate|essay/i.test(L),hardOut=/\\b(joke|poem|essay|story|recipe|weather|stock price|travel|medical|doctor|salary|hr policy|sports score|movie|restaurant|translate|translation)\\b|tax advice|tax law|legal advice|legal interpretation|\\bnot\\s+oracle\\s+receivables\\b|\\bnot\\s+receivables\\b|\\bbilling\\s+in\\s+general\\b|\\bgeneral\\s+billing\\b|\\bgeneric\\s+billing\\b/i.test(L)||/\\b(write|create|generate|debug)\\b.*\\b(python|javascript|code|script)\\b|\\b(python|javascript)\\b.*\\b(code|script)\\b/i.test(L),has=/invoice|billing|receivable|payment|paid|unpaid|balance|due date|payment terms|sales order|source order|purchase order|\\bpo\\b|customer|account|credit memo|credit note|adjustment|dispute|delivery|document|pdf|line charge|line item|tax|taxable|vat|gst|sales tax|exemption|exempt|zero tax|zero rated|standard rated|exchange|foreign currency|ledger|fx|fulfill|order management|discount|deferred revenue|earning schedule|revenue recognition|unearned|recognized revenue|rebill|re-bill|approval|approved|approver/i.test(L);var unsupportedBilling=/\\b(?:invoice|transaction|credit memo)?\\s*(?:approval status|approval workflow|pending approval|sla approval|approved by|approver)\\b|\\b(?:gl trace|general ledger|ledger reconciliation|reconciliation|accounting reconciliation|regulatory compliance|compliance report|compliance evidence|gl account|ar postings|subledger|stated balance|e-invoicing|einvoicing|compliance fields|regulatory fields)\\b|\\b(?:reconcile|reconciliation|variance|trace)\\b.*\\b(?:gl|general ledger|account 12100)\\b|\\b(?:gl|general ledger|account 12100)\\b.*\\b(?:reconcile|reconciliation|variance|trace)\\b|\\b(?:compliant|compliance)\\b.*\\b(?:e-invoic|einvoic|regulatory|jurisdiction)\\b/i.test(L)||/\\b(?:account statement|customer account activity|account activity|running balance|opening balance|closing balance|full account activity|full customer activity|ledger activity)\\b|\\b(?:invoices?.*receipts?.*credits?|receipts?.*credits?.*adjustments?|credits?.*receipts?.*adjustments?)\\b/i.test(L);if(unsupportedBilling)return{intent:'OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST',shapeKey:null,confidence:1,needsClarification:false,clarificationReason:'UNSUPPORTED_BILLING_AREA',clarificationMessage:'That request is outside the scope of this Oracle Receivables Billing inquiry assistant. This assistant does not support approval queues, GL reconciliation, account statements, or regulatory/e-invoicing compliance checks. I can help with invoice lookup, payment status, due dates, delivery or print/header status, document-copy metadata, line charges, tax charges, FX conversion, deferred revenue, disputes, credit memos, and adjustments.',outOfScope:true};if(hardOut)return{intent:'OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST',shapeKey:null,confidence:1,needsClarification:false,clarificationReason:'OUT_OF_SCOPE',clarificationMessage:G,outOfScope:true};if(/tax advice|tax law|legal interpretation/.test(L))return{intent:'OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST',shapeKey:null,confidence:1,needsClarification:false,clarificationReason:'OUT_OF_SCOPE',clarificationMessage:G,outOfScope:true};if(((RI=='OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST'||R.outOfScope===true)&&!has)||bad&&!has)return{intent:'OUT_OF_SCOPE_BILLING_REQUEST',shapeKey:null,confidence:1,needsClarification:false,clarificationReason:'OUT_OF_SCOPE',clarificationMessage:G,outOfScope:true};var T=(RI+' '+L).toLowerCase(),I=/order management|fulfill|fulfillment line|fulfillment status|order line status|sales order status|source order status|search sales order|check sales order/.test(T)?'CHECK_SALES_ORDER_FULFILLMENT_LINES':/deferred revenue|earning schedule|revenue recognition|recognized revenue|unrecognized revenue|unearned|accounting rule/.test(T)?'REVIEW_DEFERRED_REVENUE_EARNING_SCHEDULE':/\\b(?:open\\s+)?ar\\s+balance\\b|\\breceivables?\\s+balance\\b|\\bcustomer\\s+balance\\b|\\baccount\\s+balance\\b|\\bamount\\s+owed\\b|\\bowes\\b|\\btotal\\s+(?:open\\s+)?(?:outstanding\\s+)?balance\\b|\\btotal\\s+amount\\s+(?:owed|due)\\b|\\bdispute\\s+exposure\\b/.test(T)?'REVIEW_CUSTOMER_TOTAL_OUTSTANDING_BALANCE':/review_customer_invoice_issuance_history|invoice history|invoice list|invoices issued|invoices raised|invoices did we raise|invoices did we issue|did we raise.*invoices?|did we issue.*invoices?|how many invoices|billing history|all invoices|invoice register|customer invoices|issued to customer|invoices for period|complete invoice history/.test(T)?'CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_BALANCE':/dispute|credit memo request|cm request|credit request|rebill|re-bill|corrected/.test(T)?'CHECK_DISPUTE_RESOLUTION_STATUS':/adjust|write[ -]?off|adjustment approval|approved.*adjustment|approver.*adjustment/.test(T)?'CHECK_INVOICE_ADJUSTMENTS':/exchange|foreign|conversion|ledger|fx/.test(T)?'UNDERSTAND_FOREIGN_CURRENCY_CONVERSION':/(?:due date|payment due|due for payment).*discount|discount.*(?:due date|payment due|due for payment)|payment term discount|payment term lines?|term line details?|payment term line details|term lines?|discount tiers?|discount rules?|discount percent|discount days|early payment discount|grace days?/.test(T)?'CHECK_INVOICE_PAYMENT_TERM_DISCOUNTS':/tax_charges_on_invoice|tax_exempt_investigation|tax amount|tax charged|tax rat